<title>UK: Brown announces 5.5 bln stg UK fiscal tightening.</title>
<headline>Brown announces 5.5 bln stg UK fiscal tightening.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said on Wednesday that his first budget will exercise a net fiscal tightening on the economy of 5.5 billion pounds this year and 4.75 billion next.</p>
<p>&quot;I have therefore decided to tighten fiscal policy, as a result of budget measures including the windfall tax by 5.5 billion stg this year and 4.75 billion next,&quot; he told parliament in his budget speech, the first from a Labour Chancellor since 1978.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
